     "result_text_tail": "ard's \"1.4% \u2192 2.3%\" churn figure can't be rebuilt from the segment data under either weighting, so the deck uses segment churn.\n\n**Choices I made for you:**\n- **Look:** the default navy theme; I skipped the storyline review since you weren't available.\n- **10% for mid-market**, the tested level, rather than the CFO's untested 12%.\n- **8% for the SMB test**, the 2023 level.\n- **Enterprise renewals in 2027** are assumed to carry the same 60% share of capped contracts as all enterprise ARR. The pack doesn't say which contracts renew.\n- **Retention:** today's 12-month retention rates are assumed to hold for 2027. SMB's 94% may be flattered by promotion discounts ending, and the deck says so.\n\n**Checks:** QA passes with 0 fails and the renderer reports no layout problems. 105 numbers, all from the briefing pack or calculated from it, no placeholders. Two QA warnings remain only because the pack gives two numbers in words (\"about three times\", \"halve\"). The source check against web pages didn't apply, since there are no web sources. I couldn't open the deck to look at it (no converter here, and the sandbox blocks Keynote), so please flip through the slides before you present.\n\nNext, I could switch the theme, add a backup slide comparing the CFO plan and the segmented plan side by side, or rerun the numbers if you'd rather use 12% for mid-market.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- palisade-pricing-2027.pptx (20 slides)\n- palisade-pricing-2027-sources.xlsx\n- palisade-pricing-2027.json"
